  "tutorial_example_entry": {
    "lesson_index": 4,
    "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
    "lesson_core_move": "Update the Fourier series coefficients of a vertically shifted periodic signal by adding the constant offset to the DC coefficient and leaving every nonzero harmonic coefficient unchanged.",
    "section_count": 5,
    "sections": [
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "section_index": 1,
        "section_title": "Introduction to DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "step_type": "tutorial",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "tutorial_content": {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Start from a periodic signal with known trigonometric Fourier coefficients. In this form, $a_0$ is the constant or DC term, so it is the coefficient to watch when the signal is shifted vertically.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "x(t)=a_0+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}[a_n\\cos(n\\omega_0 t)+b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0 t)]",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Now form the vertically shifted signal $x_{\\text{new}}(t)=x(t)+c$. The added constant $c$ folds into the constant term, while the harmonic terms stay attached to the same cosine and sine components.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "x_{\\text{new}}(t)=x(t)+c",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "So the update rule is: add $c$ to the DC coefficient and leave every coefficient with $n\\ge 1$ unchanged. Later examples can reuse this exact notation as $a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c$, $a_n^{\\text{new}}=a_n$, and $b_n^{\\text{new}}=b_n$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c,\\qquad a_n^{\\text{new}}=a_n,\\qquad b_n^{\\text{new}}=b_n \\quad (n\\ge 1)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "section_index": 2,
        "section_title": "Adding a Positive Offset to the DC Coefficient",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "A periodic signal has trigonometric Fourier coefficients $a_0=2$, $a_1=-1$, $b_1=4$, $a_2=0$, and $b_2=-3$. The signal is shifted upward by $5$. Update the coefficient set.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is a vertical shift upward by $5$, so use the DC-update rule $a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c$. Read the original coefficient list first, then apply the offset only to $a_0$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=2+5=7",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The harmonic coefficients stay fixed: $a_1^{\\text{new}}=-1$, $b_1^{\\text{new}}=4$, $a_2^{\\text{new}}=0$, and $b_2^{\\text{new}}=-3$. So the updated coefficient set is the original list with only the DC term changed.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=7,\\qquad a_1^{\\text{new}}=-1,\\qquad b_1^{\\text{new}}=4,\\qquad a_2^{\\text{new}}=0,\\qquad b_2^{\\text{new}}=-3",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "section_index": 3,
        "section_title": "Applying a Negative Offset to the DC Coefficient",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "A periodic signal has coefficients $a_0=9$, $a_1=2$, $b_1=-1$, $a_2=-4$, and $b_2=6$. The signal is shifted downward by $3$. Update the coefficient set.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is a vertical shift downward by $3$, so treat the shift as $c=-3$ and use the same DC-update rule $a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c$. Only the constant term should move.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=9+(-3)=6",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The harmonic coefficients stay fixed: $a_1^{\\text{new}}=2$, $b_1^{\\text{new}}=-1$, $a_2^{\\text{new}}=-4$, and $b_2^{\\text{new}}=6$. So the updated coefficient set keeps every nonzero harmonic term unchanged.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=6,\\qquad a_1^{\\text{new}}=2,\\qquad b_1^{\\text{new}}=-1,\\qquad a_2^{\\text{new}}=-4,\\qquad b_2^{\\text{new}}=6",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "section_index": 4,
        "section_title": "Keeping Nonzero Harmonic Coefficients Unchanged",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "A periodic signal is shifted upward by $2$. The original coefficients are $a_0=-1$, $a_1=5$, $b_1=0$, $a_2=-2$, and $b_2=4$. Identify which coefficients change and state the updated set.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is a vertical shift upward by $2$, so treat it as $c=2$ and use the same DC-update rule $a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c$. The only coefficient that changes is the constant term.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=-1+2=1",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Copy the harmonic coefficients exactly as written: $a_1^{\\text{new}}=5$, $b_1^{\\text{new}}=0$, $a_2^{\\text{new}}=-2$, and $b_2^{\\text{new}}=4$. The zero harmonic term stays zero, and every nonzero harmonic term stays unchanged.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=1,\\qquad a_1^{\\text{new}}=5,\\qquad b_1^{\\text{new}}=0,\\qquad a_2^{\\text{new}}=-2,\\qquad b_2^{\\text{new}}=4",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 4,
        "lesson_title": "DC Adjustment from Vertical Shifting",
        "section_index": 5,
        "section_title": "Updating a Complete Fourier Coefficient Set After a Vertical Shift",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "A periodic signal has coefficients $a_0=\\tfrac{3}{2}$, $a_1=-2$, $b_1=1$, $a_2=0$, $b_2=-\\tfrac{5}{2}$, $a_3=4$, and $b_3=3$. The signal is shifted upward by $\\tfrac{7}{2}$. Update the full coefficient set and rewrite the trigonometric Fourier series.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is a vertical shift upward by $\\tfrac{7}{2}$, so use the DC-update rule $a_0^{\\text{new}}=a_0+c$. Apply the offset to the constant term first, then carry every harmonic coefficient forward unchanged.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=\\tfrac{3}{2}+\\tfrac{7}{2}=5",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Now copy the harmonic coefficients exactly: $a_1^{\\text{new}}=-2$, $b_1^{\\text{new}}=1$, $a_2^{\\text{new}}=0$, $b_2^{\\text{new}}=-\\tfrac{5}{2}$, $a_3^{\\text{new}}=4$, and $b_3^{\\text{new}}=3$. Since the series uses $a_0^{\\text{new}}/2$, the new constant term in the rewritten series is $\\tfrac{5}{2}$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_0^{\\text{new}}=5,\\qquad a_1^{\\text{new}}=-2,\\qquad b_1^{\\text{new}}=1,\\qquad a_2^{\\text{new}}=0,\\qquad b_2^{\\text{new}}=-\\tfrac{5}{2},\\qquad a_3^{\\text{new}}=4,\\qquad b_3^{\\text{new}}=3",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "x_{\\text{shifted}}(t)=\\tfrac{5}{2}-2\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+\\sin(\\omega_0 t)+0\\cos(2\\omega_0 t)-\\tfrac{5}{2}\\sin(2\\omega_0 t)+4\\cos(3\\omega_0 t)+3\\sin(3\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
